{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01744",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 5.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.08,
      "end_seconds": 9.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Afternoon, is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.27,
      "end_seconds": 16.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.47,
      "end_seconds": 24.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together. What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 25.71,
      "end_seconds": 35.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.8,
      "text": "It's pain under my right ribs after fatty meals, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.74,
      "end_seconds": 44.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.35,
      "end_seconds": 52.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "It's been going on for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.19,
      "end_seconds": 65.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.28,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.01,
      "end_seconds": 93.37,
      "duration_seconds": 24.36,
      "text": "Yes, fatty meals. That makes it worse. Only lying still, and it's not much. Honestly, a couple of times a week. I've been feeling sick too. I mean, as for feeling sick, it's mild, honestly. It comes and goes. I had pain going to my right shoulder before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.52,
      "end_seconds": 98.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Any dark urine, yellow eyes or pale stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.14,
      "end_seconds": 104.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "I haven't had dark urine, yellow eyes or pale stools, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.21,
      "end_seconds": 109.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Did you notice any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.58,
      "end_seconds": 112.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 113.97,
      "end_seconds": 118.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.5,
      "end_seconds": 125.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.93,
      "end_seconds": 132.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.28,
      "end_seconds": 136.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.13,
      "end_seconds": 143.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.18,
      "end_seconds": 145.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.83,
      "end_seconds": 151.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.67,
      "end_seconds": 162.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.09,
      "end_seconds": 167.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.39,
      "end_seconds": 179.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "I have anxiety, for about a year. I've had high blood pressure for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.46,
      "end_seconds": 183.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Right, any other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.86,
      "end_seconds": 186.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "I have heart failure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.32,
      "end_seconds": 200.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "Right, so anxiety and high blood pressure are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.01,
      "end_seconds": 204.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "My son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.24,
      "end_seconds": 220.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 222.07,
      "end_seconds": 244.25,
      "duration_seconds": 22.18,
      "text": "She is on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety, I give it to her. She is on lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day for my pressure, I give it to her. She takes metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.77,
      "end_seconds": 245.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Mm-hmm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 250.19,
      "end_seconds": 254.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "It's an antacid, 10 ml, when needed, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.84,
      "end_seconds": 273.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.82,
      "end_seconds": 278.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Ah, no, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 279.25,
      "end_seconds": 290.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. BP is 126 over 78, saturation 97 percent, pulse is 82 beats a minute, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.51,
      "end_seconds": 293.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.88,
      "end_seconds": 299.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.45,
      "end_seconds": 302.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.48,
      "end_seconds": 306.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.54,
      "end_seconds": 324.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "It is tender under the right ribs and you stop breathing in when I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.54,
      "end_seconds": 327.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.34,
      "end_seconds": 332.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.11,
      "end_seconds": 365.87,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like gallstone-related pain. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. A stomach ulcer is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.59,
      "end_seconds": 370.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.45,
      "end_seconds": 409.65,
      "duration_seconds": 38.2,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like gallstone-related pain, but I'd like to confirm. Let's book liver blood tests to look into biliary pain. I'd like to arrange an ultrasound of the abdomen for biliary pain. I'll start you on paracetamol, 1 gram, four times a day when needed, one week. That's for pain. Avoid fatty and fried foods until the scan. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.62,
      "end_seconds": 425.96,
      "duration_seconds": 11.34,
      "text": "Let's get you seen by the surgical clinic, I'll arrange the letter. Let's plan a check after the scan. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.96,
      "end_seconds": 430.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 432.01,
      "end_seconds": 433.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}